title: The KAPD Breaks in Two
subtitle: The Communist Workers' Party splits between Essen and Berlin.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 3 and kapd_exists = 1
max-visits: 1

= The KAPD Breaks in Two

The Communist Workers' Party has split. The Essen tendency around Karl Schröder wants an International of its own and no dealings with anyone. The Berlin tendency wants to keep its factory unions alive. Thousands of its workers in Berlin, Hamburg and the Ruhr are left without a home, and many of them were in our party until Heidelberg.

- @welcome: Take them back.
- @ignore: Leave them to it.

@welcome
subtitle: A few thousand old radicals return to Berlin, Hamburg and the Ruhr, with their old arguments.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('berlin', {members: 0.05, militancy: 3});
RG.district('hamburg', {members: 0.06, militancy: 3});
RG.district('ruhr', {members: 0.03});
Q.kapd_relation -= 5;
Q.lean_ultraleft += 1;
Q.unity -= 2;
!}

Whole factory groups in Neukölln and Barmbek come back to the party, and at their first district meeting they move a motion to leave the unions.

@ignore
subtitle: Nothing gained, nothing spent.
on-arrival: kapd_relation -= 3

By the end of the year the KAPD has two newspapers that attack each other more than they attack anyone else.
